#section[Professional Experience]

#table(
  columns: (1fr, auto),
  stroke: none,
  inset: 0pt,
  [
    #text(weight: "bold")[Template.net]
    \
    #text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666"))[Senior Front-End Engineer]
  ],
  [
    #align(right)[12/2020 – Present]
  ],
)

*Template.net* is an *AI-powered browser-based content creation platform* serving *10M+ users*, offering collaborative editors for graphics, documents, and whiteboards with multi-format export to *PDF*, *PNG*, and *JPEG*.

- Engineered core features for a high-performance *React*-based graphic editor, implementing drag-and-drop interactions, element transformations, and responsive visual rendering.

- Developed an AI-powered *Text-to-Design* feature that converts natural language prompts into fully editable designs.

- Implemented real-time collaborative editing with *WebSockets*, supporting concurrent users with role-based permissions for viewing, commenting, editing, and ownership.

- Architected and developed the platform homepage with *Next.js App Router*, building reusable components, shared layouts, responsive UI, and optimized rendering/data-fetching strategies.

- Built a shared *React component library* used across multiple *Micro-Frontends*, reducing duplicated code and maintaining consistent UI patterns.

- Optimized application performance using *memoization*, *virtualization*, efficient state management, and rendering optimizations for complex designs.

- Migrated the frontend from *Webpack* to *Vite* with *Module Federation*, reducing startup time by *80%* and build time by *65%*.

- Developed an internal content management platform for publishers to manage templates, categories, and digital assets, streamlining publishing workflows.

- Implemented *GitHub Actions* CI/CD pipelines to automate linting, builds, and deployments.

- Collaborated with *Product*, *Design*, and *Backend* teams on technical solutions, while mentoring junior engineers through code reviews and technical guidance.

